course: dictionary
lesson: 3214
title: Enormous and its synonyms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enormous means very, very large in size, amount or degree. It is a big word for a big thing, and it is a little stronger than just big. When you meet it, ask yourself what is so large. «Fennec foxes of the Sahara have enormous ears full of blood vessels that give off heat.» The ears are very large, so enormous means very large.
explain: Context can also show you that enormous can describe an amount, not only a size. «Deep in the Sun's core, hydrogen nuclei are squeezed together to make helium, releasing enormous energy.» Energy is not a thing you can measure with a ruler, but the sentence tells you there is a very great amount of it. Try the swap test: replace enormous with huge, and if the sentence still makes sense, you have found a synonym.
explain: Good writers choose precise words instead of piling up many big words. «We had a nice cake at the nice party and it was nice» tells us nothing. Compare «sticky», «lemony» or «lopsided», which paint a picture. Piling up «big, huge, enormous, massive, giant» just makes the reader wait for the point.
fact: Enormous means very, very large in size, amount or degree; huge.
fact: Enormous is usually not compared, so we do not normally say more enormous.
fact: Synonyms for enormous include huge, gigantic, massive, giant, vast and colossal.
fact: «Ginormous» is an informal, slangy word, so keep it for chatting, not for most writing.
fact: The Sun's core is about 15 million °C, and there hydrogen is squeezed into helium, giving out enormous energy.
exercise: «Fennec foxes of the Sahara have enormous ears.» What does enormous mean here? | *Very large | Very cold | Very fast | Very quiet
exercise: «The Sun's core releases enormous energy.» Which word could replace enormous? | Gentle | Tiny | Pale | *Huge
exercise: Why does a good writer choose «sticky» or «lemony» instead of piling up big, huge, enormous, massive? | *One precise word paints a clearer picture | Those words all mean exactly the same, so there is no reason to choose | Enormous means sticky | Long words are always better
test: «The pressure of everything above the inner core is enormous.» What does enormous mean here? | Warm | Tiny | *Very great | Thin
test: Which word is an informal, slangy way to say enormous? | Gentle | Tiny | *Ginormous | Colossal
exam: Ravi says «an enormous mess» means a very tidy room. What does enormous really mean here? | Very tidy | *A very large amount, so the mess is very big | Empty | Quiet and calm
